|~ `::tag`, the kind of a tag name, and what is declared under it: its
   constructor and its refusal, the comparisons of tag names, and
   `manifest`.
   The decisions it exists for: [D114]. ~|

:tag
  |~~ A tag names a kind, and a value carries its kind as the tag over
      it: `[1 2]` is of `::vec`, `::Box[1 2]` a vector under `::Box`.
      Taken alone, `::Box` is a value of this kind, the name a query
      asks about the kind: `::vec | doc` reads its page and
      `::vec | manifest` lists what lies under it, and `type` answers
      the tag of any value, `[1 2] | type` answering `::vec`.

      It is written `::` and a name, a slash joining names into an
      address, `::vec/count`; a tag that touches a payload puts the
      payload under it, which ::link~(::tagged | doc) tells. A kind is
      declared by its page, and its tag is the address of that name; a
      tag nothing declares is a kind of identity, which checks nothing
      and lays itself over the value. Tags rank after keywords and
      before vectors, and JSON writes a tag as its literal, `"::Box"`.
      ::snippet~(kinds) lists the kinds the scope reads, and
      ::snippet~(::Box::Crate{:a 1} | type) answers the outer tag.
      ::link~(::qlang/values | doc)
  ~~|

:tag/isATag
  |~~ A tag name is a value of `::tag`. ~~|
  ::law~(::Box | type | eq ::tag)

:tag/namesAPage
  |~~ The tag of a kind names its page. ~~|
  ::law~(5 | type | doc | type | eq ::doc)

:tag/namesNothingUndeclared
  |~~ A tag no declaration answers names no record. ~~|
  ::law~(::Unbound[1] | type | binding !| type | eq ::any/binding/UnknownNameError)

:tag/construct
  |~~ Reads a tag name as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/PayloadNotTagError
  |~~ `::tag` reads its payload as the tag name it is; a value's own
      tag is read by `type`.
  ~~|

:tag/construct/readsATagNameAsItself
  |~~ `::tag` over a tag name is that name. ~~|
  ::law~(::tag::Box | eq ::Box)

:tag/PayloadNotTagError/refusesAKeyword
  |~~ A keyword payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::tag:k !| [type (get /actualType)] | eq [::tag/PayloadNotTagError ::keyword])

:tag/gt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes after the tag name
      the call gives, `::b | gt ::a`. Tag names compare by their names as
      they are spelled, letter by letter, so a capital comes before a
      small letter, `::a | gt ::B` answering `true`, and a name comes
      before the names that go on under it, `::vec/count | gt ::vec`
      answering `true`; values sorted by `type` so fall in the order of
      the names of their kinds. A tag name compares with a tag name
      alone: a keyword, a string or any other value given is refused
      under the value, `::status | gt :open` among them. `gte` answers
      whether the subject comes after the value or is the same name,
      `lt` and `lte` the reverse.
      ::link~(::tag/gte | doc) ::link~(::tag/lt | doc)
      ::link~(::tag/lte | doc) ::link~(::keyword/gt | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | gt ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/NotTagError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | gt ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `gt` of keywords, `:b | gt :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value, `false`
            otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | law :ordersByName |~~ `::b` comes after `::a`. ~~| ~(::b | gt ::a)
    | law :putsACapitalFirst
        |~~ A capital comes before a small letter. ~~| ~(::a | gt ::B)
    | law :putsANameBeforeTheNamesUnderIt
        |~~ A name comes before the names that go on under it. ~~|
        ~(::vec/count | gt ::vec)
    | law :keepsOneNameApartFromItself
        |~~ A name does not come after itself. ~~| ~(::a | gt ::a | not)
    | law :ordersValuesByTheNamesOfTheirKinds
        |~~ Values sorted by `type` fall in the order of the names of
            their kinds.
        ~~|
        ~([1 "a" :k] | sort ~(type) | eq [:k 1 "a"])
    | law :value/NotTagError/refusesAKeyword
        |~~ A keyword is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::a | gt :a !| type | eq ::tag/gt/value/NotTagError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/gte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes after the tag name
      the call gives or is the same name, `::b | gte ::b`. It compares as
      `gt` does, tag names with tag names, by their names as they are
      spelled.
      ::link~(::tag/gt | doc) ::link~(::tag/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | gte ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/NotTagError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | gte ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `gte` of keywords, `:b | gte :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value or is the same
            name, `false` otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | law :holdsOfItself
        |~~ A name comes after or is itself. ~~| ~(::b | gte ::b)
    | law :keepsAnEarlierNameApart
        |~~ An earlier name does not come after a later one. ~~|
        ~(::a | gte ::b | not)
    | law :value/NotTagError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::b | gte 1 !| type | eq ::tag/gte/value/NotTagError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/lt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes before the tag name
      the call gives, `::a | lt ::b`. It compares as `gt` does, tag names
      with tag names, by their names as they are spelled, so `::B | lt
      ::a` answers `true`.
      ::link~(::tag/gt | doc) ::link~(::tag/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | lt ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/NotTagError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | lt ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `lt` of keywords, `:b | lt :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value, `false`
            otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | law :ordersByName |~~ `::a` comes before `::b`. ~~| ~(::a | lt ::b)
    | law :putsACapitalFirst
        |~~ A capital comes before a small letter. ~~| ~(::B | lt ::a)
    | law :keepsOneNameApartFromItself
        |~~ A name does not come before itself. ~~| ~(::a | lt ::a | not)
    | law :value/NotTagError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::b | lt 1 !| type | eq ::tag/lt/value/NotTagError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/lte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes before the tag name
      the call gives or is the same name, `::a | lte ::a`. It compares as
      `gt` does, tag names with tag names.
      ::link~(::tag/lt | doc) ::link~(::tag/gte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | takes :value
        |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against
            the subject, `::b | lte ::a`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::tag
    | throws :value/NotTagError
        |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | lte ::a`; a keyword
            compares by the `lte` of keywords, `:b | lte :a`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value or is the same
            name, `false` otherwise.
        ~~|
        ::boolean
    | law :holdsOfItself
        |~~ A name comes before or is itself. ~~| ~(::a | lte ::a)
    | law :ordersByName |~~ `::a` comes before `::b`. ~~| ~(::a | lte ::b)
    | law :value/NotTagError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
        ~(::b | lte 1 !| type | eq ::tag/lte/value/NotTagError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/manifest
  |~~ Answers the set of the names declared one name under the noun the
      subject names, each by its address: `::number | manifest` the
      words and the refusals of numbers, `::vec/take | manifest` the
      parts and the answer of `take`, `::qlang | manifest` the chapters
      of the language. A tag name that names nothing answers the empty
      set. The laws of a name are no part of the answer, `laws` reads
      them; the kinds of the scope `kinds` lists, and what the reader
      declared `env`; and what one name holds the axes read,
      `::vec/count | source`, `| doc`. The subject is the tag name of the
      noun: a keyword, `:number`, names a binding and no noun, and is
      refused as any other value is, and the call takes no value, so
      `manifest ::vec` is refused.
      ::snippet~(::number | manifest) ::link~(::any/laws | doc)
      ::link~(::any/kinds | doc) ::link~(::any/env | doc)
      ::link~(::any/source | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns
        |~~ The addresses of the names declared one name under the noun. ~~|
        ::set
    | throws :SubjectNotTagError
        |~~ `manifest` is asked of a noun by its tag name, `::number |
            manifest`; a keyword names a binding and no noun.
        ~~|
    | throws :ArgsBeyondPartsError
        |~~ `manifest` reads the noun of the subject and takes no value:
            the manifest of vectors is `::vec | manifest`.
        ~~|
    | law :holdsAVerbOfTheNoun
        |~~ The manifest of numbers holds `add`. ~~|
        ~(::number | manifest | has ::number/add)
    | law :holdsAChapter
        |~~ The manifest of the first page holds its chapter on values. ~~|
        ~(::qlang | manifest | has ::qlang/values)
    | law :holdsThePartsOfAWord
        |~~ The manifest of a word holds its parts. ~~|
        ~(::vec/take | manifest | has ::vec/take/count)
    | law :holdsTheNamesOfAReader
        |~~ The manifest of a reader's noun holds the names declared under
            it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/area ~(1) | ::Box | manifest | eq #[::Box/area])
    | law :leavesTheLawsToLaws
        |~~ The laws of a name are no part of its manifest. ~~|
        ~(::number/add | get [(manifest | filter ~(binding | get /value | is ::law) | count) (laws | count | gt 0)] | eq [0 true])
    | law :answersNothingForANameThatNamesNothing
        |~~ A tag name that names nothing answers the empty set. ~~|
        ~(::Nothing | manifest | eq #[])
    | law :SubjectNotTagError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no noun. ~~|
        ~(5 | manifest !| [type (get /actualType)] | eq [::tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError ::number])
    | law :SubjectNotTagError/refusesAKeyword
        |~~ A keyword names a binding and no noun. ~~|
        ~(:number | manifest !| type | eq ::tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError)
    | law :ArgsBeyondPartsError/refusesANounGivenAsAValue
        |~~ A noun given as a value is refused; it is the subject. ~~|
        ~(::qlang | manifest ::vec !| type | eq ::tag/manifest/ArgsBeyondPartsError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/toString
  |~~ Answers the name of the tag as a string, `::vec | toString`
      answering `"vec"`, so a kind joins text. `toTag` turns the name
      back into the tag.
      ::link~(::string/toTag | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The name of the tag, a string. ~~| ::string
    | law :answersTheName
        |~~ A tag answers its name. ~~|
        ~([::vec ::number/add] | map ~toString | eq ["vec" "number/add"])
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/toKeyword
  |~~ Answers the keyword of the tag's name, `::Box | toKeyword`
      answering `:Box`, as `groupBy ~(type)` files values by their kinds.
      `toTag` turns the keyword back into the tag.
      ::link~(::keyword/toTag | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The keyword of the tag's name. ~~| ::keyword
    | law :readsBack
        |~~ A tag turned into its keyword turns back into itself. ~~|
        ~(::Box | toKeyword | toTag | eq ::Box)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:tag/toTag
  |~~ Answers the tag itself, so `map ~toTag` turns names and tags into
      tags, `["vec" :Box ::map] | map ~toTag` answering
      `[::vec ::Box ::map]`.
      ::link~(::string/toTag | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The tag itself. ~~| ::tag
    | law :answersItself
        |~~ A tag answers itself, so names and tags turn into tags. ~~|
        ~(["vec" :Box ::map] | map ~toTag | eq [::vec ::Box ::map])
    | impl ::builtin{}

